{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nImplement the accepted scope from architecture recommendations 2, 4, and 6, following the evidence on `expecting-renowned-buzzard`.\n\nCurrent `origin/main` still has three related sources of protocol complexity:\n\n- Reconciler `Mutation` has typed direction/action but a generic `Mapping[str, Any]` payload. Outbound typed mutations are converted through `_mutation_to_batch_dict()` into the legacy batch shape; two CREATE shapes and a polymorphic `applier.apply()` remain.\n- `PydanticAIRunner.run()` has regrown after ADR 0056. Existing ownership seams already include `ProviderSession`, `model_classes`, `structured_run`, `agent_call`, `runner_support`, capability modules, and ordered success/failure telemetry. The next change must improve those boundaries, not duplicate them.\n- ADR 0098's `OperationSnapshot` is authoritative for reconciler runtime bindings, but CLI/shared command paths still call `emit_shadow_snapshot()`, and many LLM operations independently resolve `LLMConfig.from_env()`.\n\nThis epic completes these migrations. It extends ADR 0103 rather than reopening its retry/coordinator decision, works within ADRs 0056 and 0058 unless the runner research child proves an amendment is needed, and completes ADR 0098's expand/contract migration.\n\n## Outcomes\n\n### A. One typed reconciler representation and one production route\n\nDefine payload types as a discriminated union by `(direction, action)`, carry them through planner/coordinator/adapter boundaries, prove behavior against a broad corpus in side-effect-free shadow mode, then cut production over and delete dictionary translation and legacy dispatch in this epic. Deletion is part of the cutover, not a follow-up.\n\n### A1. Reconciler runway and producer inputs\n\nRestore <=700-line headroom in the uncovered spine modules, then eliminate the loose 24-value\nproducer seam using Brant/RP-03 types and owners—never a second generic context.\n\n### B. Runner lifecycle ownership grounded in current architecture\n\nFirst produce a current effect/resource timeline and fault matrix. Then reshape only call-graph seams that the evidence supports, preserving `ProviderSession` as provider-resource owner, fallback `ExitStack` ordering, failure accounting, pre-finalization success logging, final spend/result-shape updates, provider provenance, and existing injection contracts.\n\nNo new function-NLOC ratchet or per-file headroom gate is in scope. ADR 0058's single 800-LOC ceiling remains the hard gate and debt signal. The reconciler's one-time prerequisite extractions restore room under that existing gate; they do not create another enforcement mechanism. Any future function-size metric requires separate evidence and approval.\n\n### C. Authoritative operation configuration\n\nMake the existing `OperationSnapshot` and focused runtime bindings behavior-bearing at the CLI, MCP, Python, shared command/store, and LLM operation boundaries. An operation composes once; downstream code consumes projections/context and cannot reread environment, files, or CWD. Remove diagnostic shadow composition and migrated ambient-resolution paths after parity.\n\n## Verification strategy\n\n- Portable/default-CI: replay a versioned synthetic and scrubbed-store corpus through legacy and typed planning/serialization without executing either against Jira. Compare canonical normalized intents, outcomes, diagnostics, ordering, idempotence, and final modeled state.\n- Ephemeral Jira DC: extend the existing `tests/external/live_jira_dc` harness, its no-remote scrubbed store copy, multi-project scratch fixtures, and comprehensive mutation table. Run the exact implementation patchset in CI against disposable projects/instances. Legacy and typed paths must never dual-send to the same target: compare isolated projects or fresh instances, normalize generated keys/timestamps, re-observe final state, and run a typed-only convergence pass after deletion.\n- Runner: inject failures before/after provider construction, fallback entry, external call, result finalization, and each telemetry/accounting boundary; assert close order, no duplicate effect, and preserved accounting/provenance.\n- Configuration: consumer-level metamorphic tests mutate environment/config/CWD after composition; the active operation's outputs/effects remain unchanged while a new operation observes the change.\n\nThe Jira DC lane is additive evidence, not the only gate: the portable synthetic oracle must run without a CI provider or external service. No project's live Jira environment or credentials may be reachable from these tests.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- No production dual-write/double-send comparison.\n- Reuse the existing ephemeral Jira DC harness and isolation assertions; do not build a second DC test environment.\n- Preserve Jira Cloud behavior with verified fakes/transport contracts even though large-scale live mutation testing uses disposable DC.\n- Reuse `OperationSnapshot`, central schema/provenance, `LLMRuntime`, `ProviderSession`, and current runner leaf modules; no second config schema, generic hook bus, plugin framework, or decorative frozen lifecycle carriers.\n- Reuse reconciler `Observation`, `TicketPlan`, and current pass/runtime owners; no generic option-bag replacement.\n- String imports, monkeypatch targets, and compatibility re-exports require a census before movement/deletion.\n- New structural decisions complete the ADR lifecycle before dependent implementation; accepted ADRs are constraints, not prose to reimplement.\n- Keep every intermediate Gerrit change independently testable and green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every supported reconciler `(direction, action)` has one typed payload contract, and planners, coordinator, adapters, manifest/diagnostic code, and tests consume it without generic action payload dictionaries.\n- [ ] The portable shadow corpus covers create/update/delete/probe/conflict, inbound-only actions, links/comments/labels/status/parent/binding fields, retries/ambiguous outcomes, malformed inputs, suppression/follow-ons, and multi-project routing; legacy and typed normalized traces match or every intentional delta is documented and approved.\n- [ ] An exact-patchset ephemeral Jira DC CI run proves large-scale isolated differential parity and typed-only post-deletion convergence without any route to the project's live Jira or ticket remote.\n- [ ] `_mutation_to_batch_dict`, polymorphic legacy `apply` selection, duplicate CREATE shapes, and obsolete compatibility dispatch/re-exports are deleted in this epic; one production route remains.\n- [ ] Runner research records the current ownership/effect timeline and an ADR disposition before refactoring; implementation reuses established seams, preserves lifecycle/telemetry order under the fault matrix, and adds no function-size or per-file headroom gate.\n- [ ] CLI, MCP, Python, shared command/store, and LLM operations compose one authoritative snapshot/context; behavior-bearing consumers do not reread ambient configuration during the operation.\n- [ ] Diagnostic shadow composition and migrated legacy resolution paths are deleted, with structural ownership checks and consumer-level metamorphic tests preventing reintroduction.\n- [ ] Existing focused suites, the full default suite, lint, typecheck, complexity/module-size gates, portable reconciler oracles, and the Jira DC lane pass; documentation and ADR status match the landed architecture.\n- [ ] `reconcile.py` and `reconcile_helpers.py` are each <=700 LOC through cohesive deletion/extraction; the lifecycle facade and ADR 0099 repair boundary remain guarded.\n- [ ] No mutation producer retains or repackages the 24-value outbound-update bundle; stages use cohesive Brant/RP-03 inputs.\n- [ ] Final epic evidence reports deleted representations/routes/ambient authorities and demonstrates that no cleanup item was deferred solely to keep both old and new paths live."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788055422063631006,"uuid":"82f72466-c065-40c6-925f-5548362a4bc9"}